; ECP bus UART-style RX for VISTA-Panel-Tool (RP2040 PIO port)
;
; Confirmed via oscilloscope (cursor timing): the ECP bus runs 4800 baud,
; 8 data bits, even parity, 2 stop bits (8E2). The software bit-bang
; decoder (ECPSoftwareSerial.cpp, an interrupt-driven port of
; Dilbert66/esphome-components' ESP8266/ESP32 library) works fine when
; the bus is quiet, but reliably loses sync partway through the one long
; (44-byte, ~100ms) continuous read once real bus traffic overlaps it
; (bench-confirmed: fails specifically once a physical keypad's own
; activity interleaves with the panel's status broadcast) -- consistent
; with an occasional missed GPIO edge in the CPU-interrupt-driven bit
; sampler under load. Moving byte assembly onto a PIO state machine
; removes CPU/interrupt latency from the timing path entirely: PIO
; samples GPIO with cycle-accurate hardware timing regardless of what the
; CPU is doing.
;
; The "wait for start bit / center on first data bit / shift in 8 bits"
; front half below is reused unmodified from the Raspberry Pi Pico SDK's
; own uart_rx.pio reference example (proven, not reinvented here). Only
; the tail differs, to match this bus's actual 8E2 framing instead of
; plain 8-N-1: the original checks a single stop bit and conditionally
; pushes; this version pushes unconditionally (via autopush, once 8 bits
; land) and then just waits out the parity bit + 2 stop bits (3 bit-times)
; before re-arming for the next start bit, without validating them.
; Skipping parity validation here deliberately matches how the existing
; software decoder already treats a parity mismatch as non-fatal --
; checkParity() in ECPSoftwareSerial.cpp only printf()s a warning and
; still keeps the byte, so doing the same (nothing at all) in PIO loses
; no real protection.
;
; Clock: configure so 8 PIO cycles = 1 bit time (matching the per-bit
; loop cadence below), i.e. clkdiv = clock_get_hz(clk_sys) / (8.0f * baud).
; sm_config_set_in_shift(&c, true /* shift right, LSB first */,
;                         true /* autopush */, 8 /* threshold */) --
; matching the stock example's own proven config exactly. With that
; config, each assembled byte lands in bits 31:24 of the FIFO word
; (the stock example's own documented behavior); read it back with
; `pio_sm_get(pio, sm) >> 24`.

.program ecp_uart_rx

start:
    wait 0 pin 0        ; stall until the start bit (falling edge)
    set x, 7    [10]    ; 8 data bits to collect; delay centers us on data bit 0
bitloop:
    in pins, 1          ; autopush fires automatically once the 8th bit lands
    jmp x-- bitloop [6] ; ~8 cycles/iteration; collects all 8 data bits, LSB first
    nop         [23]    ; skip parity bit + 2 stop bits (3 bit-times = 24 cycles), unchecked
